1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Here!

2
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:11,319
Hsu Wei-zhe.

3
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:13,640
What's wrong with you?
Playing ball outside?

4
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:16,238
Wei-zhe, are you listening?

5
00:00:16,239 --> 00:00:17,520
An-an, stop!

6
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:23,039
- That was close.
- It's red now. Air quality is level four.

7
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:24,399
Let him play for a bit…

8
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:25,319
Come here.

9
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:27,399
No, we're indoors.

10
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:28,999
- No, go in.
- Let him play.

11
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,159
I'll hit you. Air's bad. Why play?

12
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:32,799
Exercise is good for him too.

13
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,319
Kids gotta play, right?

14
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:35,760
- And relapse?
- Hey!

15
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:50,600
Again?

16
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:52,680
I swear it's true, okay?

17
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:57,080
What are you watching?

18
00:00:57,840 --> 00:00:59,240
Nothing juicy.

19
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:07,480
They sleep apart and live separate lives.

20
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:10,360
Never seen them intimate.

21
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:14,400
I'm watching
how he takes care of his wife.

22
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:17,080
I take care of you too, okay?

23
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:21,160
All you do is talk.

24
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:23,320
I do everything.

25
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,800
Why wait so long?

26
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:37,360
I couldn't reach you.

27
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:39,879
I thought something happened.

28
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:42,880
No, I had to be sure first.

29
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:45,319
Or you'll say I'm dreaming.

30
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:47,360
You are. You're dreaming.

31
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:51,800
First,

32
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,440
I'm taking the chance God gave us.

33
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:56,759
Second,

34
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:59,159
it's a chance
to leave for somewhere better.

35
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:00,439
Would you give it up?

36
00:02:00,440 --> 00:02:03,999
- I wouldn't.
- No.

37
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,639
We're supposed to pretend to be them
and face their families and friends?

38
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:09,119
Won't they notice

39
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:10,879
something's wrong?

40
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:13,359
And how will we survive?

41
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:16,439
An-an, how will you explain
his sudden return?

42
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:18,599
What about your mom?

43
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:19,520
Have you…

44
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:21,479
thought this through?

45
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:23,359
You think I haven't?

46
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:25,760
You haven't thought it through.
That's why.

47
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:35,239
I've got it figured out.

48
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:36,719
I'll find a way for you--

49
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:38,000
I think…

50
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:41,959
this place will improve in a few years.

51
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:46,359
- Two years of this, you're still hopeful?
- Can you guarantee he'll get better?

52
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,840
What if he gets worse?

53
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:50,399
Trust me.

54
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:52,959
The air is better there.
An-an will be better.

55
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,159
I just need more time

56
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:55,999
- with that family--
- Hsu Wei-zhe,

57
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,719
please focus your talents on making money.

58
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:00,399
- Stop dreaming.
- Money again?

59
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:02,799
I'm trying.

60
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:05,079
Everything I do is for you guys.

61
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:06,199
For you guys.

62
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:09,560
It's all on the phone, a gift from God.
Check it yourself.

63
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:11,680
I'm smoking.

64
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:20,439
<i>Here's more news on the haze.</i>

65
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:25,719
<i>The Disaster Center issued a rare
Level 6 Air Quality Alert, sparking panic.</i>

66
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:29,359
<i>The Weather Bureau says
air quality is worsening fast</i>

67
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:33,759
<i>and urges everyone to stay indoors
if an alert is received.</i>

68
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:38,679
<i>Extra caution is advised for kids
with epilepsy or asthma.</i>

69
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:40,759
If kids show any unusual symptoms,

70
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:45,280
<i>put an anti-smog mask on them right away
and head to…</i>

71
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:50,639
Is he still coughing badly?

72
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:52,159
The phone's there.

73
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:55,199
- Call a ride. We're going to the hospital.
- Okay.

74
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,320
Let's go.

75
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:58,760
Call a ride.

76
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:50,120
Mom!

77
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:04,320
I can't hear…

78
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:18,400
Go wait at the door
for Mei-ling and An-an.

79
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:28,640
You saw it, right?

80
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:32,719
HIS DAD'S A GOOD MAN.
I'LL COME PICK YOU UP THIS AFTERNOON.

81
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:33,840
Did you see it?

82
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,959
I'll go over this afternoon.

83
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:38,880
This afternoon.

84
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:58,160
I think she did.

85
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,160
<i>Wei-zhe!</i>

86
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:03,240
<i>Wei-zhe.</i>

87
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:08,200
Hello?

88
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:10,280
<i>I fell down.</i>

89
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:12,920
Are you okay?

90
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:15,319
<i>I can't move.</i>

91
00:08:15,320 --> 00:08:16,679
<i>Come down now.</i>

92
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:17,800
Coming down.

93
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:57,759
An-an, wake up.

94
00:08:57,760 --> 00:08:58,760
Come on.

95
00:09:00,680 --> 00:09:02,279
Wake up.

96
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:03,360
What happened?

97
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,279
Be quiet.

98
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:06,599
Put this on.

99
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:07,760
Here.

100
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:43,840
Where are we going?

101
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:48,920
- Where's Dad?
- Quiet.

102
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:56,519
Where are you going? Come on, hurry.

103
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:58,640
- Dad's not coming…
- Keep quiet.

104
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:07,120
Come on.

105
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:10,280
<i>Jian-cheng?</i>

106
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,440
Jian-cheng?

107
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:17,120
Jian-cheng?

108
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:35,080
Jian-cheng? Where are you?

109
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,120
Jian-cheng!

110
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:09,560
Mom.

111
00:11:11,160 --> 00:11:12,800
Where are you going this late?

112
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:22,480
An-an,

113
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,519
let's go to bed.

114
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:25,560
Come on.

115
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:27,440
Come on.

116
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:29,600
Sleep with Mom.

117
00:11:42,880 --> 00:11:44,280
Did the mirror crack?

118
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:53,400
I called for you. Where were you?

119
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:56,999
I had an urgent work issue to handle.

120
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,760
I found my chair screws were loose,

121
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:01,600
so I went downstairs for a screwdriver.

122
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:06,240
Did I miss… something?

123
00:12:52,680 --> 00:12:53,760
I'm home.

124
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:01,320
Running this early?

125
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:05,160
Running here with such good air

126
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:07,760
feels better than the gym.

127
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:16,520
I had a realization. Want to hear it?

128
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:19,920
Here's my thought.

129
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:23,280
Where there is sunlight,

130
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:25,160
there are shadows.

131
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:29,120
<i>We can choose</i>

132
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,600
<i>to leave them behind</i>

133
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:34,200
<i>and look ahead.</i>

134
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:37,920
<i>The light will guide our way.</i>

135
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:41,520
<i>Just push ahead.</i>

136
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,480
<i>A new future awaits.</i>

137
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:47,840
<i>How was that?</i>

138
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:54,480
- How did you say something so inspiring?
- See?

139
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:58,919
A coworker sent me
this motivational message.

140
00:13:58,920 --> 00:14:00,320
Said it boosts energy.

141
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:09,840
You smell like smoke.

142
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:13,040
Why?

143
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:14,720
Really?

144
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:16,800
I'll shower.

145
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:19,599
Ran into a coworker.

146
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:20,599
A heavy smoker.

147
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:24,199
By the way, we see Dr. Jian at 2:00 p.m.

148
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:26,799
You go first. I'll come later.

149
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:29,519
My laptop needs repairs,

150
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:32,040
and I have important files
to send tonight.

151
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:33,800
Sure.

152
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:36,720
Smells great.

153
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:38,879
I knew it.

154
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:40,919
I knew it would…

155
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:43,760
I told you.

156
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:49,960
I knew he'd get better.

157
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:52,119
Stop scratching.

158
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:54,840
- It won't heal if you pick it.
- It itches.

159
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:57,400
You have to put up with it.

160
00:15:58,840 --> 00:16:01,160
Stop scratching. Be patient. Come here.

161
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:05,600
Come on. Get dressed.

162
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:07,800
Learn to apply your own medicine.

163
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:09,919
You have to grow up.

164
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:12,880
I don't want to grow up.
I want to stay with you.

165
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:16,480
We'll always be together.

166
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:18,720
Grow up safe and healthy.

167
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,560
Okay?

168
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:28,160
Dad!

169
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:30,239
Go eat breakfast.

170
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:31,399
Time for school.

171
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:32,480
Sure.

172
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:50,440
You're moving.

173
00:16:52,560 --> 00:16:53,840
Is that enough stuff?

174
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:57,120
I don't get it.

175
00:16:58,720 --> 00:16:59,920
His mom isn't going?

176
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:03,960
You're leaving her here?

177
00:17:09,079 --> 00:17:11,160
She called me to the basement last night

178
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:14,640
so you could secretly take An-an away,

179
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:17,240
right?

180
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:25,720
Is my wife

181
00:17:27,359 --> 00:17:28,480
still alive?

182
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:31,400
- Wei-zhe won't hurt her.
- Says who?

183
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:34,000
Have you seen her?

184
00:17:36,280 --> 00:17:37,800
I know your plan.

185
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,800
You want to leave

186
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:42,160
and take our identities.

187
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:49,279
An-an has always been fragile.

188
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:51,480
A simple cold can trigger his asthma.

189
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:53,799
The air's getting worse.

190
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:56,199
Many children, including An-an,
have epilepsy.

191
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,799
Some have even died from it.

192
00:17:57,800 --> 00:18:01,520
We have respiratory diseases
and kids with asthma there too.

193
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:05,400
Every season brings
different deadly viruses.

194
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:07,880
Is it that difficult?

195
00:18:09,080 --> 00:18:12,439
If parents protect their kids,
they'll be fine.

196
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:15,199
You don't live here
so you don't know our pain.

197
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:17,680
I don't know yours
because I've never lost a child.

198
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:23,439
- Did the mirror crack?
- I don't know.

199
00:18:23,440 --> 00:18:25,279
- Why didn't you go?
- I don't know.

200
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:26,559
- Why?
- I don't know.

201
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:30,560
- Why…
- I don't know.

202
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:33,799
The mirror cracks
at 2:00 p.m. and 2:00 a.m.

203
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:35,999
It's a short window, but it didn't open.

204
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,679
I want to know why too!

205
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:39,719
Why didn't it open?

206
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:41,040
I really want to know!

207
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,080
HIS DAD'S A GOOD MAN.
I'LL COME PICK YOU UP THIS AFTERNOON.

208
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:41,280
What happened?

209
00:19:43,400 --> 00:19:45,480
Take me out when the rain stops.

210
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:51,840
You haven't taken me out in a long time.

211
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:10,240
No jacket or mask?

212
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:13,759
You said you only had 15 minutes.

213
00:20:13,760 --> 00:20:15,680
I rushed over and forgot my jacket.

214
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:18,320
What's the rush?

215
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:22,600
You said you were leaving.

216
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:24,680
Sounded like for good.

217
00:20:25,840 --> 00:20:27,480
Thought I'd never see you again.

218
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:32,160
My home is here. Of course I'd come back.

219
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:33,920
Is that it?

220
00:20:38,840 --> 00:20:40,240
Let's talk in the car.

221
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:45,560
You kept dodging coffee this month.

222
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:47,920
Driving you and An-an home,

223
00:20:48,640 --> 00:20:51,120
you seemed like
a totally different person.

224
00:20:55,680 --> 00:21:00,040
Your wife never looked happy
when I brought An-an in.

225
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:03,400
I'm divorcing her.

226
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:11,600
I never forgot you.

227
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:28,960
Would you leave him?

228
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:31,759
I know it's been hard--

229
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:35,280
I only saw you as a friend.
I shouldn't have told you.

230
00:21:36,040 --> 00:21:37,400
Just friends?

231
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:42,560
I know you feel something.

232
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:47,319
The kids are young.

233
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:49,679
This divorce will hurt them deeply.

234
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:51,759
They're young.

235
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:53,959
They adapt quickly.

236
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:57,480
As long as home is peaceful,
they'll grow up happy.

237
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:08,920
I can give you the life you want.

238
00:22:09,760 --> 00:22:13,160
With me, you don't have to work
or take exams.

239
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:15,800
I'll look after you and An-an.

240
00:22:20,920 --> 00:22:22,880
Treat him as my own.

241
00:22:29,080 --> 00:22:31,160
- An-an loves his father.
- And you?

242
00:22:35,640 --> 00:22:37,440
If you could choose again,

243
00:22:39,320 --> 00:22:40,640
would you choose him?

244
00:22:47,120 --> 00:22:49,600
We argued sometimes,

245
00:22:50,600 --> 00:22:52,880
but he never said sorry.

246
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:56,360
He showed it through actions.

247
00:22:57,240 --> 00:22:58,680
But last night,

248
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:02,320
he apologized.

249
00:23:04,440 --> 00:23:05,520
Also,

250
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:09,440
I feel like some of his habits
have changed.

251
00:23:10,160 --> 00:23:13,280
The strange thing is
I smelled cigarette smoke on him.

252
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:16,040
I suspect he's been smoking.

253
00:23:16,640 --> 00:23:17,720
He's not a smoker.

254
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:22,679
Did I tell you he doesn't smoke?

255
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:24,960
Yes, you told me before.

256
00:23:25,600 --> 00:23:28,200
He quit because Yoo-shin
hated the smell of smoke.

257
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:33,319
Also,

258
00:23:33,320 --> 00:23:36,559
he never used to go running
early in the morning.

259
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:40,159
Then a few months ago, he joined a gym

260
00:23:40,160 --> 00:23:42,920
near your Taipei clinic.

261
00:23:43,480 --> 00:23:44,599
Such a coincidence?

262
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:45,640
Yes.

263
00:23:46,320 --> 00:23:48,920
Maybe he went to the gym to avoid me.

264
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:55,640
<i>After work, he could go to the gym
and then stay at his dad's place.</i>

265
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:59,760
<i>Sometimes he came home,</i>

266
00:24:00,520 --> 00:24:02,720
<i>but he would just stay in his room.</i>

267
00:24:05,440 --> 00:24:06,560
<i>For years,</i>

268
00:24:08,160 --> 00:24:11,599
<i>I couldn't give him
the attention he needed.</i>

269
00:24:11,600 --> 00:24:14,040
<i>I know he was hurting and unhappy.</i>

270
00:24:15,600 --> 00:24:17,280
He changed

271
00:24:19,960 --> 00:24:21,960
after he started going to the gym.

272
00:24:29,040 --> 00:24:31,120
I think there's someone else.

273
00:24:32,560 --> 00:24:35,640
<i>I'm afraid he's going to leave me.</i>

274
00:24:37,240 --> 00:24:40,319
<i>He took time off</i>

275
00:24:40,320 --> 00:24:41,760
<i>and apologized.</i>

276
00:24:42,440 --> 00:24:45,520
That shows he wants
to fix your relationship.

277
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:49,120
He's changed so much.

278
00:24:51,640 --> 00:24:52,800
<i>I wonder…</i>

279
00:24:54,880 --> 00:24:56,680
<i>if he is even Jian-cheng.</i>

280
00:25:41,960 --> 00:25:43,040
Mei-ling?

281
00:25:44,360 --> 00:25:45,520
Mei-ling?

282
00:26:04,600 --> 00:26:05,680
Mom?

283
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:10,760
Mom!

284
00:26:34,160 --> 00:26:35,199
Hello?

285
00:26:35,200 --> 00:26:36,800
<i>Mei-ling, where's my mom?</i>

286
00:26:38,800 --> 00:26:41,039
Wei-zhe? You're back?

287
00:26:41,040 --> 00:26:43,640
<i>Where's my mom? Where's that guy?</i>

288
00:26:45,840 --> 00:26:48,079
<i>What are you doing? Where did my mom go?</i>

289
00:26:48,080 --> 00:26:51,159
<i>What are you doing?
Where'd she go? Answer me!</i>

290
00:26:51,160 --> 00:26:52,200
<i>Hello?</i>

291
00:26:53,800 --> 00:26:55,119
I don't know.

292
00:26:55,120 --> 00:26:56,839
I was at work. Beats me.

293
00:26:56,840 --> 00:26:58,040
<i>What do you mean?</i>

294
00:26:58,600 --> 00:27:00,000
<i>Did you tie him up?</i>

295
00:27:01,120 --> 00:27:02,799
I did. He untied himself--

296
00:27:02,800 --> 00:27:04,159
My mom is missing.

297
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:05,359
Where did he take her?

298
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:07,559
<i>- I don't know!</i>
- Are you insane?

299
00:27:07,560 --> 00:27:08,719
What if she gets hurt?

300
00:27:08,720 --> 00:27:11,159
You're crazy…

301
00:27:11,160 --> 00:27:12,600
You're…

302
00:27:36,320 --> 00:27:38,600
It's getting late. Let's go back.

303
00:27:40,760 --> 00:27:41,920
I'm not going back.

304
00:27:46,040 --> 00:27:47,320
I want warm milk.

305
00:27:54,880 --> 00:27:55,960
Happy?

306
00:27:57,600 --> 00:27:59,960
I'll take you out every day there.

307
00:28:03,080 --> 00:28:05,480
Go without me. I'm old.

308
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:09,680
I can still live on my insurance here.

309
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:12,200
If I go there, I'll have nothing.

310
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:14,680
I'll only become a burden.

311
00:28:15,600 --> 00:28:18,840
You have me. You're not alone.

312
00:28:22,320 --> 00:28:23,960
Are you worried about him?

313
00:28:27,120 --> 00:28:31,040
I checked. They're different, okay?

314
00:28:32,600 --> 00:28:34,240
<i>I have no identity there.</i>

315
00:28:35,280 --> 00:28:36,960
<i>Where would you hide me?</i>

316
00:28:38,280 --> 00:28:39,360
<i>In the basement?</i>

317
00:28:53,360 --> 00:28:55,160
I have a plan. Okay?

318
00:28:56,440 --> 00:28:58,400
I'll tell you when we get there.

319
00:29:00,280 --> 00:29:01,680
Can you trust me this once?

320
00:29:02,360 --> 00:29:04,680
Take care of your wife and child.

321
00:29:05,680 --> 00:29:07,440
Let me go peacefully.

322
00:29:10,400 --> 00:29:12,480
I don't want to burden you anymore.

323
00:29:15,840 --> 00:29:17,400
Treat Mei-ling well.

324
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:21,200
I've had enough

325
00:29:23,280 --> 00:29:24,760
from this life.

326
00:29:41,360 --> 00:29:42,440
Not going in?

327
00:29:43,240 --> 00:29:44,640
I don't want to go in.

328
00:29:45,600 --> 00:29:47,680
I don't want to stay inside.

329
00:29:59,600 --> 00:30:01,120
Put on your mask anyway.

330
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:12,640
Wei-zhe?

331
00:30:24,080 --> 00:30:25,120
Forget it.

332
00:30:49,720 --> 00:30:50,879
Hey.

333
00:30:50,880 --> 00:30:51,880
Hey!

334
00:30:52,600 --> 00:30:54,559
You came alone?

335
00:30:54,560 --> 00:30:56,040
Mei-ling isn't with you?

336
00:31:02,440 --> 00:31:03,520
My mom's with me.

337
00:31:04,840 --> 00:31:07,280
Being a good son today?

338
00:31:15,520 --> 00:31:16,560
Package pickup.

339
00:31:17,440 --> 00:31:19,080
- Last three digits.
- 845.

340
00:31:22,760 --> 00:31:23,760
Hey.

341
00:31:24,320 --> 00:31:26,080
Treat Mei-ling better.

342
00:31:54,800 --> 00:31:56,040
Mom!

343
00:32:22,960 --> 00:32:25,759
<i>Oxcarbazepine,
a drug with fewer side effects,</i>

344
00:32:25,760 --> 00:32:28,999
<i>is facing severe supply shortages.</i>

345
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:32,879
<i>Panicked parents
are flooding the FDA with calls.</i>

346
00:32:32,880 --> 00:32:36,999
<i>Officials say it isn't the only option
for childhood epilepsy,</i>

347
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:39,319
<i>urging parents to stay calm</i>

348
00:32:39,320 --> 00:32:41,759
<i>and avoid unverified sources.</i>

349
00:32:41,760 --> 00:32:44,320
<i>Doctors will offer alternatives, but…</i>

350
00:32:51,560 --> 00:32:52,960
You're late today.

351
00:32:54,280 --> 00:32:56,240
Do I need to tell you where I go?

352
00:33:02,880 --> 00:33:04,760
Why take my mother-in-law out?

353
00:33:06,080 --> 00:33:07,200
She wanted to go.

354
00:33:10,480 --> 00:33:11,600
That obedient?

355
00:33:13,720 --> 00:33:16,800
She lied about a boy
who looked like An-an.

356
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:20,319
She sent me away

357
00:33:20,320 --> 00:33:21,880
and stepped into the road.

358
00:33:23,320 --> 00:33:24,559
She wanted to die.

359
00:33:24,560 --> 00:33:26,120
- Is she injured?
- No.

360
00:33:26,760 --> 00:33:27,840
She's sleeping.

361
00:33:28,880 --> 00:33:31,440
I'm the one suffering. PTSD.

362
00:33:34,480 --> 00:33:36,160
If anything happened to her,

363
00:33:36,960 --> 00:33:38,800
Wei-zhe would hate me forever.

364
00:33:39,520 --> 00:33:41,560
If he really cared about his mom,

365
00:33:42,640 --> 00:33:44,440
why keep her in the basement?

366
00:33:48,200 --> 00:33:49,320
What do you know?

367
00:33:50,480 --> 00:33:52,160
The conditions here are bad.

368
00:33:52,880 --> 00:33:55,879
The basement is cooler in summer
and warmer in winter.

369
00:33:55,880 --> 00:33:58,199
She can't go outside

370
00:33:58,200 --> 00:33:59,920
and get hit by a car.

371
00:34:00,560 --> 00:34:01,560
That's abuse.

372
00:34:02,560 --> 00:34:03,600
"Abuse"?

373
00:34:04,280 --> 00:34:06,639
Do you know how much I do every day?

374
00:34:06,640 --> 00:34:08,279
I work, deliver, cook,

375
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:09,760
and care for her every day.

376
00:34:10,360 --> 00:34:11,999
You call this abuse?

377
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:15,000
She's sick and takes so many pills!

378
00:34:15,639 --> 00:34:17,879
She could've been free,

379
00:34:17,880 --> 00:34:19,919
but Wei-zhe insisted on a tracheostomy!

380
00:34:19,920 --> 00:34:20,919
Wish she had died?

381
00:34:20,920 --> 00:34:23,360
Yes. I wish she had died.

382
00:34:23,960 --> 00:34:25,479
Look at how she's suffering!

383
00:34:25,480 --> 00:34:28,559
Ease her pain
and maybe she'd want to live.

384
00:34:28,560 --> 00:34:29,719
Who are you to say that?

385
00:34:30,440 --> 00:34:31,600
Who are you?

386
00:34:32,880 --> 00:34:35,360
Don't like it? Leave. Get out!

387
00:34:41,080 --> 00:34:42,999
- An-an, it's okay.
- Can I help?

388
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:44,559
Mom's here.

389
00:34:44,560 --> 00:34:47,400
It's okay…

390
00:37:03,520 --> 00:37:04,720
I'm back.

391
00:37:16,120 --> 00:37:17,520
I'm back.

392
00:37:33,520 --> 00:37:35,400
I waited forever for the parts.

393
00:37:36,400 --> 00:37:38,160
You were gone when I arrived.

394
00:37:38,840 --> 00:37:40,480
Dr. Jian had patients,

395
00:37:41,560 --> 00:37:42,960
so I didn't interrupt.

396
00:37:43,640 --> 00:37:44,879
How was it?

397
00:37:44,880 --> 00:37:46,080
Was your talk okay?

398
00:37:53,840 --> 00:37:55,880
I got your favorite, spicy diced chicken.

399
00:38:04,200 --> 00:38:05,160
Come.

400
00:38:06,480 --> 00:38:07,560
Have some.

401
00:38:23,480 --> 00:38:25,880
- The mirror just now--
- What happened to it?

402
00:38:27,920 --> 00:38:30,200
I saw Yoo-shin in the mirror again.

403
00:38:33,200 --> 00:38:34,800
He called you "Faye-bo's dad."

404
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:37,800
Do you remember…

405
00:38:42,200 --> 00:38:46,080
when he started calling you that?

406
00:38:53,040 --> 00:38:54,160
I think…

407
00:39:01,680 --> 00:39:05,080
it began when I told him about Fibonacci.

408
00:39:08,720 --> 00:39:11,720
He didn't want toys.

409
00:39:13,920 --> 00:39:15,840
He just wanted to play number games.

410
00:39:30,040 --> 00:39:31,240
I miss those days.

411
00:39:34,280 --> 00:39:37,200
We took turns adding
the previous two numbers.

412
00:39:39,280 --> 00:39:40,600
It took a lot of time

413
00:39:42,160 --> 00:39:43,320
and effort,

414
00:39:44,840 --> 00:39:46,040
but those were

415
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:48,359
happy moments,

416
00:39:48,360 --> 00:39:49,600
just for us.

417
00:39:53,160 --> 00:39:54,240
Yeah.

418
00:39:55,240 --> 00:39:59,160
You two always made my head spin
with the counting.

419
00:40:00,120 --> 00:40:01,480
I don't quite remember

420
00:40:02,680 --> 00:40:04,600
how many digits

421
00:40:05,240 --> 00:40:07,240
you got to last time.

422
00:40:37,640 --> 00:40:39,000
Probably six digits.

423
00:40:41,840 --> 00:40:43,999
<i>He made us start over when we were wrong.</i>

424
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:47,040
If he knew I'd been faking mistakes
since four digits,

425
00:40:49,640 --> 00:40:51,000
would he hate me?

426
00:41:12,680 --> 00:41:13,800
You eat first.

427
00:41:17,280 --> 00:41:19,040
I'll be right back.

428
00:41:41,560 --> 00:41:43,159
I should've known.

429
00:41:43,160 --> 00:41:45,280
Why didn't I see it?

430
00:41:48,640 --> 00:41:49,760
Honey?

431
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:52,240
You coming out soon?

432
00:42:03,520 --> 00:42:04,960
You know I have a key.

433
00:42:10,720 --> 00:42:11,840
Tell me

434
00:42:13,080 --> 00:42:14,160
what I got wrong.

435
00:42:15,120 --> 00:42:17,279
I searched everywhere

436
00:42:17,280 --> 00:42:19,959
for "FIBO, Fibonacci sequence."

437
00:42:19,960 --> 00:42:22,840
I had no damn clue what it was.

438
00:42:24,040 --> 00:42:25,720
Sorry for the language.

439
00:42:33,680 --> 00:42:34,760
Don't worry.

440
00:42:35,480 --> 00:42:36,840
I won't use the key.

441
00:42:37,920 --> 00:42:40,720
I know it's rude.

442
00:42:41,800 --> 00:42:43,280
Please come out yourself,

443
00:42:43,880 --> 00:42:44,880
okay?
